pendell@hotmail.com wrote:
> Description:  Alchemists and/or shopkeepers are aware that people
> sometimes rob their stashes. As a result, they will secrete "booby
> traps" to ensure that anyone foolish enough to simply chug their
> potions will suffer a nasty end.

Bad idea.  This would completely discourage players from testing
potions by drinking by making it potentially fatal in normal cases,
which would be against the basic spirit of the game dating back to
Rogue.  There is only one random item in the game that testing through
its primary use is lethal, and it's an amulet, which is not exactly the
most common item type anyway.  (Wands of Death don't count since you
would test those against monsters, not yourself.)

The fact that ID-by-experimentation is not a strategy that is used by
many experienced players is, in my view, one of the problems with the
more recent versons of Nethack.  (Maybe I'm just masochistic, but I'm
really hoping they do something about price ID'ing in the next
version.)

